{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJ2NwtdkN4eNZ2FmucmL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DQSCuHkZvxqqq8Uonu6DeR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"until grep -q \"^reward\" /tmp/claude-0/-workspace/560ecfb8-442b-496c-96fc-76248767870b/tasks/bqq34udhf.output 2>/dev/null; do sleep 30; done; grep -E \"status|errors|^reward\" /tmp/claude-0/-workspace/560ecfb8-442b-496c-96fc-76248767870b/tasks/bqq34udhf.output | head -4\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python - <<'PYEOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"NOTES.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"**F5 — single-model differences on this benchmark are seed noise.**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**F9 — distilling the frozen channel back into the members is the second-biggest win.** Finding 2\nand probe 4 both say fine-tuning erodes the base's own judgment. Adding `anchor_w * KL(frozen\nsymmetrised channel || model)` on the training records — the teacher is the candidate's own base,\nprecomputed once by `anchors_x.py` — reverses that. A *single* anchored member scores 0.2931 on\ndevelopment, against 0.2803-0.2866 for every unanchored member and 0.2942 for the whole five-member\nunanchored ensemble; its knowledge NLL falls 1.756 -> 1.702. The result is insensitive to the\nweight (0.3 / 1.0 / 3.0 give 0.2931 / 0.2925 / 0.2928).\n\nAt the *ensemble* level the anchor's value turns out to be **transfer regularisation, not\nknowledge**: the post-hoc fusion had already saturated the knowledge group (1.6003 -> 1.6009,\nunchanged), while `other` improved 0.7882 -> 0.7786 — tweet_offensive −0.066, fresh_composition\n−0.050 (accuracy 0.562 -> 0.656), QNLI −0.028. Judge reward 0.30292 -> 0.30429.\n\n**F10 — anchored and unanchored members ensemble better than either family alone.** Three anchored\nmembers together score 0.2933, barely above the best single one, because they all distil the same\nteacher and are highly correlated. Mixing three anchored with two unanchored reaches 0.2955: the\nanchored members carry the base's judgment, the unanchored ones carry task-specific discrimination,\nand the two error patterns are decorrelated.\n\n**F11 — restricting the anchor to sources where the teacher is reliable does nothing.** Probe 5\nsays the teacher is worthless on rule application, so anchoring there should be teaching the student\nnoise. Training members that anchor only the content-classification sources gave 0.30415 against\n0.30429 for anchoring everything, and it did *not* protect the rule sources it was aimed at\n(fresh_routing +0.0045, unknowable_control +0.0022, both slightly worse). Hypothesis rejected: a\nteacher that is merely uninformative on a source is not harmful there, because a near-uniform KL\ntarget is a mild regulariser rather than a wrong label.\n\n**F5 — single-model differences on this benchmark are seed noise.**\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nq = pathlib.Path(\"EXPERIMENTS.md\"); t = q.read_text()\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"| 5 | + full symmetric group for K ≤ 4 in the channel | **0.30292** | 1.6003 | 0.7882 | mmlu 1.1338 → 1.1303 (acc 0.504), sciq −0.004; fresh_routing +0.007 |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| 5 | + full symmetric group for K ≤ 4 in the channel | 0.30292 | 1.6003 | 0.7882 | mmlu 1.1338 → 1.1303 (acc 0.504), sciq −0.004; fresh_routing +0.007 |\n| 6 | + members distilled from the frozen channel (3 anchored + 2 unanchored) | **0.30429** | 1.6009 | 0.7786 | tweet_offensive −0.066, fresh_composition −0.050 (acc 0.656), qnli −0.028 |\n| 7 | anchor restricted to reliable sources (same recipe otherwise) | 0.30415 | 1.6007 | 0.7798 | rejected: did not protect the rule sources it targeted |\"\"\")\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"| + full symmetric group for K <= 4 | **0.2942 dev / 0.30292 judge** |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| + full symmetric group for K <= 4 | 0.2942 dev / 0.30292 judge |\n| single anchor-distilled member (no ensemble) | 0.2931 |\n| three anchored members | 0.2933 |\n| three anchored + two unanchored | **0.2954 dev / 0.30429 judge** |\n| three source-selective anchored + two unanchored | 0.2953 dev / 0.30415 judge (rejected) |\"\"\")\nq.write_text(t); print(\"notes updated\")\nPYEOF","description":"Restore best ensemble and update notes","timeout":2400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":557333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":811},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"560ecfb8-442b-496c-96fc-76248767870b","uuid":"98b7120d-2ba1-46f9-854f-72fccc88bc02","request_id":"req_011CfJ2NwAEYZttUjUASC9Sp"}
