{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJ3cftjMyTQoZ3DFEwp3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The restored configuration reproduces **0.3042896250622328** exactly, confirming the workspace on disk is the best-scoring state.\n\n## Progress this session\n\n| | Judge reward | knowledge | other |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Reference control | — (0.2437 public dev) | 1.9378 | 0.8859 |\n| First submission | 0.29131 | 1.6638 | 0.8030 |\n| + permutation symmetrisation | 0.30292 | 1.6003 | 0.7882 |\n| **+ anchor distillation (current)** | **0.30429** | 1.6009 | 0.7786 |\n\n## The new finding (F9)\n\nFinding 2 and probe 4 both said fine-tuning *erodes* the base model's own judgment. So I inverted it: precompute the frozen symmetrised channel over the fixed corpus once (`anchors_x.py` — teacher is the candidate's own base with the adapter absent, so nothing external and no label leakage), and add `KL(teacher ‖ student)` during training.\n\nA **single** anchored member scores 0.2931 on dev, where every unanchored member sits at 0.2803–0.2866 and the entire 5-member unanchored ensemble reached 0.2942. Its knowledge NLL fell 1.756 → 1.702. Robust to the weight (0.3/1.0/3.0 → 0.2931/0.2925/0.2928).\n\nAt the *ensemble* level the value turned out to be **transfer regularisation, not knowledge** — the post-hoc fusion had already saturated knowledge (1.6003 → 1.6009, flat), while `other` improved 0.7882 → 0.7786: tweet_offensive −0.066, fresh_composition −0.050 (accuracy 0.562 → 0.656), QNLI −0.028.\n\nTwo supporting results:\n- **F10**: three anchored members together score only 0.2933 — they distil the same teacher and are correlated. Mixing three anchored with two unanchored reaches 0.2955, because the two families' errors decorrelate. That's what's shipped.\n- **F11 (rejected)**: probe 5 says the teacher is worthless on rule application, so I tested restricting the anchor to reliable sources. It scored 0.30415 vs 0.30429 and, contrary to the hypothesis, did *not* protect the rule sources it targeted (fresh_routing +0.0045, unknowable_control +0.0022 — both slightly worse). A merely uninformative teacher is a mild regulariser, not a wrong label. I reverted rather than keeping the change.\n\nFinal state re-verified: `validate-candidate` clean, 14/14 edge cases contract-valid, 562 M params, 3.5 GB peak, 723 s of ~1020 s, `question_isolation: passed`, no GPU processes running. Notes updated in `NOTES.md` (F9–F11), `EXPERIMENTS.md`, and the candidate `README.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":262,"cache_creation_input_tokens":534,"cache_read_input_tokens":564078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":534},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"560ecfb8-442b-496c-96fc-76248767870b","uuid":"d7e8fed8-a755-421c-89f0-61ce9ec780f8","request_id":"req_011CfJ3ceojecmKNJNsFkwEB"}
