{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJ8b8AK8UTiNrD2kFrpB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final state verified and locked in.\n\n## Result\n\n**Judge reward 0.30429** (best of 8 submissions), from a reference control of 0.2437 on public development — a 25% relative improvement.\n\n| | Judge | knowledge | other |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Submission 1 | 0.29131 | 1.6638 | 0.8030 |\n| + permutation symmetrisation | 0.30292 | 1.6003 | 0.7882 |\n| **+ anchor distillation (shipped)** | **0.30429** | 1.6009 | 0.7786 |\n\n564 M params, 3.5 GB peak, 723 s of ~1020 s, `question_isolation: passed`, 14/14 edge cases valid, no GPU processes running.\n\n## This round: four hypotheses tested, four rejected\n\nI pushed on every remaining lever I could construct a mechanism for, and none survived:\n\n- **Longer training with the anchor** (F12): four epochs scored 0.2927 vs 0.2931 at two. The anchor *does* remove the over-adaptation penalty that Finding 2 identified — unanchored training had collapsed 0.2813 → 0.2641 over the same range — but flat is not a gain.\n- **Full anchor coverage** (dropping option-set augmentation so no target is skipped): 0.2924. No better.\n- **Ensemble size, composition and weighting** (F13): six members 0.2949–0.2956 vs five at 0.2955. A fitted continuous family weight *looked* better (0.2964 at the grid edge), but the discrete composition sweep contradicted its direction — so that number was a one-parameter fit to dev noise, and I discarded it. The shipped 3-anchored/2-unanchored split sits inside a flat optimum.\n- **A second frozen channel** (probe 6): cloze likelihood carries real but weaker signal (+9.1% on multi-way choice vs the letter channel's +19.0%). Fused without constraint it reached 0.2960 — by placing its weight in precisely the two buckets that fail my ≥2% reliability gate, the signature of noise-fitting. Gated honestly, it gains 0.0012 macro-nll from one extra scalar, twelve times below the ~0.015 standard error, at the cost of an extra forward pass per option.\n\nThat last one is the clearest case of the discipline this benchmark demands: an unconstrained search will always find a few thousandths, and the gate I built for the letter channel (Finding 8) caught it doing so. I rejected it on the criterion I'd already written down rather than banking the number.\n\nThe system is at a genuine plateau. Knowledge sits within ~0.04 nats of the frozen base's own ceiling, and the remaining `other` error is concentrated in boolean-rule and date-arithmetic families where a 0.5B single forward pass has no skill and the calibration correctly converges on near-uniform. Notes updated with probe 6 and F12–F13."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1573,"cache_read_input_tokens":587817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1573},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"560ecfb8-442b-496c-96fc-76248767870b","uuid":"1a6b6d75-3d5e-4edb-806f-60aa4b069bd8","request_id":"req_011CfJ8b6pgtSWrQ1LiRNphX"}
