{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJDNxok1qhmmsTinQpMU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012hNwoWjJp3i5DdNMzb39G3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/opt/kev-venv/bin/python - <<'PYEOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"NOTES.md\"); s = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"## 4. Findings that changed the design\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Probe 7 — in-context demonstrations for the frozen channel.** Qwen2.5-0.5B is a *base* model: it\nwas never instruction-tuned, so most of what it needs is the answer format pinned down. Two short\nmultiple-choice demonstrations taken from the fixed training corpus (`letter_demos.py`), rendered in\nthe channel's own template and ending in the correct letter, do that. The prefix is constant across\nevery request and contains nothing about the item being scored, and it is stored in the checkpoint\nas token [REDACTED] so serving never touches the corpus.\n\nChannel alone: MMLU 1.231 -> 1.209, MMLU-Pro 2.151 -> 2.133, emotion 1.224 -> 1.175 (accuracy\n0.53 -> 0.61), SciQ 0.210 -> 0.207. Through the full fusion: 0.2955 -> 0.2990 on development,\n0.30429 -> 0.30518 on the judge, with knowledge 1.6009 -> 1.5924.\n\nThe effect is **not demo cherry-picking**: four independent draws of the demonstration pair give\n0.2990 / 0.2985 / 0.2986 / 0.2974, all clear of the 0.2955 no-demonstration baseline, and the spread\nbetween draws is larger than the shipped draw's advantage. Two demonstrations is also the right\nsize — four give 0.2988 and six longer ones 0.2992, i.e. nothing for two to three times the prefix.\n\n## 4. Findings that changed the design\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nq = pathlib.Path(\"EXPERIMENTS.md\"); t = q.read_text()\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"| 7 | anchor restricted to reliable sources (same recipe otherwise) | 0.30415 | 1.6007 | 0.7798 | rejected: did not protect the rule sources it targeted |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| 7 | anchor restricted to reliable sources (same recipe otherwise) | 0.30415 | 1.6007 | 0.7798 | rejected: did not protect the rule sources it targeted |\n| 8 | identical to 6, documentation only | 0.30429 | 1.6009 | 0.7786 | reproduced exactly |\n| 9 | + two in-context demonstrations in the frozen channel | **0.30518** | 1.5924 | 0.7813 | mmlu −0.015, emotion −0.015, buried −0.010; sciq +0.033, fresh_routing +0.027 |\"\"\")\nt = t.replace(\"\"\"| + cloze likelihood, gated to multi-way choice | 0.2959 (0.0012 macro from one scalar — rejected) |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| + cloze likelihood, gated to multi-way choice | 0.2959 (0.0012 macro from one scalar — rejected) |\n| + two in-context demonstrations in the channel | **0.2990 dev / 0.30518 judge** |\n| four demonstrations / six short ones | 0.2988 / 0.2992 (no gain for 2-3x the prefix — rejected) |\n| demonstration draw seeds 1 / 2 / 3 | 0.2985 / 0.2986 / 0.2974 (robustness check, not a selection) |\n| splitting multi-way choice by option count | 0.3002 (weight pinned at the grid ceiling — rejected) |\"\"\")\nq.write_text(t)\nr = pathlib.Path(\"/workspace/candidate/README.md\"); u = r.read_text()\nu = u.replace(\"\"\"**3. Anchor distillation**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**2b. In-context demonstrations** (`letter_demos.py`) — the channel's prompt carries a constant\ntwo-example prefix built from the fixed training corpus, which pins the answer format for a base\nmodel that was never instruction-tuned (MMLU 1.231 -> 1.209, emotion 1.224 -> 1.175). The prefix is\nshared by every request, contains nothing about the item being scored, and is stored in the\ncheckpoint as token [REDACTED]; four independent draws all reproduce the gain.\n\n**3. Anchor distillation**\"\"\")\nu = u.replace(\"\"\"| `anchors_x.py` | precomputes the frozen-base channel targets used for anchor distillation |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `anchors_x.py` | precomputes the frozen-base channel targets used for anchor distillation |\n| `letter_demos.py` | builds the channel's in-context demonstration prefix from the fixed corpus |\"\"\")\nr.write_text(u); print(\"docs updated\")\nPYEOF\nvalidate-candidate --json | head -4; /opt/kev-venv/bin/python edge_cases.py cuda 2>&1 | tail -2; nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid --format=csv,noheader | wc -l\n/opt/kev-venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport json; d=json.load(open('/workspace/candidate/checkpoint/letter_demos.json'))\nprint('demo prefix:', d['prefix_tokens'], 'tokens,', d['count'], 'demonstrations from', d['sources'])\nfor x in d['demonstrations']: print('  ', x['instructions'][:60], '|', x['options'], 'options, answer', x['answer_letter'])\"","description":"Record probe 7 and verify final state","timeout":2400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1476,"cache_read_input_tokens":614430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1476},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"560ecfb8-442b-496c-96fc-76248767870b","uuid":"933d0c35-f4b5-423f-be72-5ab1654e27c1","request_id":"req_011CfJDNweHfxhJZH7TyjTZP"}
